  "comment": "Baseline re-registered by hand (90,000 -> 63,800 ticks/s). Throughput fell 29% since 2026-08-26; attributed by profiling the SAME workload at four commits with an identical 49,196 worker passes in each, which put the whole regression in ONE step rather than across the 51 commits between: the indicator centralisation (#517, +1.54s worker self-time \u2014 Wilder's RMA is the standard definition and reads five periods of history where the old inline RSI read one) plus the per-tick equity sample (#497, +0.18s, what makes the drawdown tick-exact in both pipelines). Both are correctness bought with throughput, both chosen knowingly. A vectorised closed form for the two exponential averages already took back 5.0% of tick-run time (interleaved wall-clock A/B, no overlap between groups) and this baseline is measured WITH it. Warmup unchanged (6.5 -> 6.6s) is the control proving the machine and the disk are not the cause.",
